IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g9-interpretation`
IMPORT `g9-common`

-- g9-sched2-tribunal.l4: Schedule 2 to the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, headed "Charity Commission tribunal" (Article 32; Article 32 and Article 1 call the body the Charity Tribunal): the appointment
-- and termination of its members, its staff, resources and reporting, and its procedure. Quotations are copied by srcrefs.py from the text of the Law (src:N is line N of that file) and every rule carries an @ref.
-- Schedule 2 is parallel to Schedule 1 and its figures are NOT the same (trap T20): the notice of resignation is one month, not 3 months (2(1)(a)); the absence is longer than 8 weeks, not 4 (2(2)(a)).
-- It is written out in full beside Schedule 1 and not shared with it: each rule below names its own figure, and the helpers it calls are the counting rules of g9-common.l4, which take the figure as an argument.
-- Roles: the Minister, the States and the Charity Tribunal are constructors of `Legal actor`; a member of the tribunal and the responsible officer are not (nouns request in FRAGMENT-G9.md),
-- so `Role under Schedule 2` is a stand-in, used only for what a member or the responsible officer does.
-- A discretion of the Minister ("appearing to the Minister to be suitable", "satisfying himself or herself", "considers are required") is an INPUT.

§ `Schedule 2: Charity Commission tribunal (Article 32)`

-- The heading of Schedule 2 reads "Charity Commission tribunal"; Article 32(1) establishes "a tribunal to be known as the Charity Tribunal" and Article 1 defines the tribunal accordingly.
-- The heading is not operative: it names the same body (see the contradictions in FRAGMENT-G9.md).
-- src:812 | Schedule 2
-- src:813 | (Article 32)
-- src:814 | Charity Commission tribunal
@ref Schedule 2 (heading) (src:812-814)
`Sch 2 the heading Charity Commission tribunal (inert)` MEANS
    "Schedule 2 (Article 32) Charity Commission tribunal"

§§ `The acts of Schedule 2`

DECLARE `Role under Schedule 2` IS ONE OF
    `a member of the tribunal under Schedule 2`
    `the responsible officer of the tribunal under Schedule 2`

-- Each act names who does it: the first actor of an act is its performer (an actor may only perform its own acts).
DECLARE `Act under Schedule 2` IS ONE OF
    `Sch 2: appoint a person as a member of the tribunal` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 2: seek the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission on an appointment as a member of the tribunal` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 2: present to the States a notice of intention to appoint a person as a member of the tribunal` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 2: determine the period of an appointment as a member of the tribunal` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 2: re-appoint a person serving as a member of the tribunal` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 2: designate one member of the tribunal as the chair and another as the vice-chair` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 2: determine that the chair or all the members of the tribunal are to be remunerated by the States` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 2: terminate the appointment of a member of the tribunal` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 2: present to the States a notice that the Minister has terminated the appointment of a member of the tribunal` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 2: make staff and resources available to the tribunal` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 2: secure that a member of staff is available to the tribunal as the responsible officer` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 2: lay a copy of the report on the tribunal before the States` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 2: regulate the procedure of the tribunal` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 2: make Regulations on the procedure of the tribunal` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 2: make Regulations creating an offence in relation to the tribunal` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`

DECLARE `Act of a member or the responsible officer under Schedule 2` IS ONE OF
    `Sch 2: resign from the tribunal by notice in writing to the Minister` HAS by IS A `Role under Schedule 2`
    `Sch 2: prepare a report on the activities of the tribunal` HAS by IS A `Role under Schedule 2`
    `Sch 2: provide the Minister with the report on the tribunal` HAS by IS A `Role under Schedule 2`

`Sch 2: the Minister appoints a person as a member of the tribunal` MEANS `Sch 2: appoint a person as a member of the tribunal` `the Minister`
`Sch 2: the Minister seeks the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission on the appointment of a member` MEANS `Sch 2: seek the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission on an appointment as a member of the tribunal` `the Minister`
`Sch 2: the Minister presents a notice of intention to the States to appoint a member` MEANS `Sch 2: present to the States a notice of intention to appoint a person as a member of the tribunal` `the Minister`
`Sch 2: the Minister determines the period of the appointment of a member` MEANS `Sch 2: determine the period of an appointment as a member of the tribunal` `the Minister`
`Sch 2: the Minister re-appoints a member serving` MEANS `Sch 2: re-appoint a person serving as a member of the tribunal` `the Minister`
`Sch 2: the Minister designates the chair and the vice-chair` MEANS `Sch 2: designate one member of the tribunal as the chair and another as the vice-chair` `the Minister`
`Sch 2: the Minister determines that the chair or all the members are to be remunerated` MEANS `Sch 2: determine that the chair or all the members of the tribunal are to be remunerated by the States` `the Minister`
`Sch 2: the Minister terminates the appointment of a member` MEANS `Sch 2: terminate the appointment of a member of the tribunal` `the Minister`
`Sch 2: the Minister presents a notice of the termination of a member to the States` MEANS `Sch 2: present to the States a notice that the Minister has terminated the appointment of a member of the tribunal` `the Minister`
`Sch 2: the Minister makes staff and resources available to the tribunal` MEANS `Sch 2: make staff and resources available to the tribunal` `the Minister`
`Sch 2: the Minister secures a responsible officer for the tribunal` MEANS `Sch 2: secure that a member of staff is available to the tribunal as the responsible officer` `the Minister`
`Sch 2: the Minister lays a copy of the report on the tribunal before the States` MEANS `Sch 2: lay a copy of the report on the tribunal before the States` `the Minister`
`Sch 2: the tribunal regulates its own procedure` MEANS `Sch 2: regulate the procedure of the tribunal` `the Charity Tribunal`
`Sch 2: the States make Regulations on the procedure of the tribunal` MEANS `Sch 2: make Regulations on the procedure of the tribunal` `the States`
`Sch 2: the States make Regulations creating an offence in relation to the tribunal` MEANS `Sch 2: make Regulations creating an offence in relation to the tribunal` `the States`
`Sch 2: a member resigns by notice in writing` MEANS `Sch 2: resign from the tribunal by notice in writing to the Minister` `a member of the tribunal under Schedule 2`
`Sch 2: the responsible officer prepares the report` MEANS `Sch 2: prepare a report on the activities of the tribunal` `the responsible officer of the tribunal under Schedule 2`
`Sch 2: the responsible officer provides the Minister with the report` MEANS `Sch 2: provide the Minister with the report on the tribunal` `the responsible officer of the tribunal under Schedule 2`

§§ `1 Appointment`

-- What the Law fixes about one appointment, or re-appointment, of a member of the tribunal (1(6): references in paragraph 1 to appointment include re-appointment).
DECLARE `Appointment of a member of the tribunal` HAS
    `the day of the appointment` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the Minister makes the appointment (or re-appointment)
    `the first day of the term` IS A DATE @desc The first day on which the person is a member under this appointment
    `the day the term expires` IS A DATE @desc The end date of the period determined by the Minister under paragraph 1(5)
    `the person appears to the Minister to be suitable for the position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Minister's opinion under paragraph 1(1): an input, not computed
    `the person appears to the Minister to have appropriate experience to safeguard the interests of the public and the charitable sector in Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Minister's opinion under paragraph 1(1): an input, not computed
    `the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The day on which the Minister sought the views (paragraph 1(2)); NOTHING if never
    `a notice of intention was presented to the States on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The day on which the Minister presented the notice (paragraph 1(3)); NOTHING if never
    `the person was serving as a member of the tribunal on the day of the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE for a re-appointment of a person serving (paragraph 1(6))
    `the term is followed by a re-appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE where the person is re-appointed when this term expires, so that the expiry is not "without re-appointment" (paragraph 2(4)(a))
    `the day on which the person became a member of the States` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc NOTHING if the person is not a member of the States (paragraph 2(4)(b))
    `the service before this appointment` IS A LIST OF `Period of service under the Schedules` @desc The periods of service as a member of the tribunal before this appointment, earliest first (paragraph 2(4)(c))

-- src:816 | (1) The Minister must appoint as members of the tribunal at least 4, and no more than 8, persons appearing to the Minister to be suitable for the position and to have appropriate experience to safeguard the interests of the public and the charitable sector in Jersey.
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 1(1) (src:816)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 2 para 1(1) the Minister must appoint at least this many members of the tribunal` MEANS 4

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 1(1) (src:816)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 2 para 1(1) the Minister must appoint no more than this many members of the tribunal` MEANS 8

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 1(1) (src:816)
@export Whether the number of members of the tribunal is within the limits of paragraph 1(1): at least 4 and no more than 8
GIVEN `the number of members of the tribunal` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of persons who are members of the tribunal on the day in question
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 1(1) the number of members of the tribunal is within the limits` `the number of members of the tribunal` MEANS
        `the number of members of the tribunal` AT LEAST `Sch 2 para 1(1) the Minister must appoint at least this many members of the tribunal`
    AND `the number of members of the tribunal` AT MOST `Sch 2 para 1(1) the Minister must appoint no more than this many members of the tribunal`

-- The duty to have at least 4 members. The Law states no day by which the members must be appointed, so the duty stands while there are fewer than 4.
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 1(1) (src:816)
@export The Minister's duty to appoint at least 4 suitable and experienced members of the tribunal
GIVEN `the number of members of the tribunal` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of persons who are members of the tribunal on the day in question
      appointment IS AN `Appointment of a member of the tribunal` @desc The appointment or re-appointment, with the dates of its steps and the facts that bear on its expiry
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 2`
`Sch 2 para 1(1) the Minister must appoint at least 4 persons appearing to be suitable and to have appropriate experience as members of the tribunal` `the number of members of the tribunal` appointment MEANS
    IF `the number of members of the tribunal` AT LEAST `Sch 2 para 1(1) the Minister must appoint at least this many members of the tribunal`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the Minister`
         MUST `Sch 2: the Minister appoints a person as a member of the tribunal`
         PROVIDED     appointment's `the person appears to the Minister to be suitable for the position`
                  AND appointment's `the person appears to the Minister to have appropriate experience to safeguard the interests of the public and the charitable sector in Jersey`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not appoint at least 4 persons appearing to the Minister to be suitable for the position and to have appropriate experience as members of the tribunal"

-- The limit of 8: a ninth appointment is a breach.
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 1(1) (src:816)
@export The prohibition on the Minister's appointing more than 8 members of the tribunal
GIVEN `the number of members of the tribunal` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of persons who are members of the tribunal on the day in question
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 2`
`Sch 2 para 1(1) the Minister must not appoint more than 8 members of the tribunal` `the number of members of the tribunal` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    SHANT `Sch 2: the Minister appoints a person as a member of the tribunal`
    PROVIDED `the number of members of the tribunal` AT LEAST `Sch 2 para 1(1) the Minister must appoint no more than this many members of the tribunal`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister appointed a ninth member of the tribunal: no more than 8 persons may be appointed"

-- The parenthesis of 1(2), "without prejudice to the powers of the States or the Jersey Appointments Commission under Article 15 of that Law", preserves those powers and adds no rule here.
-- src:817 | (2) Before appointing a person as a tribunal member, the Minister must seek the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission established by Article 17 of the Employment of States of Jersey Employees (Jersey) Law 2005 on the appointment (without prejudice to the powers of the States or the Jersey Appointments Commission under Article 15 of that Law).
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 1(2) (src:817)
@export The Minister's duty to seek the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission before appointing a tribunal member, with the last day for it
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      `the day of the appointment` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the appointment (or re-appointment) is made
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 2`
`Sch 2 para 1(2) before appointing a person as a tribunal member the Minister must seek the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission` interp `the day of the appointment` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MUST `Sch 2: the Minister seeks the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission on the appointment of a member`
    BEFORE (`Sch 1 and 2: the latest day for the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission to be sought` interp `the day of the appointment`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not seek the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission before appointing a person as a tribunal member"

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 1(2) (src:817)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
      appointment IS AN `Appointment of a member of the tribunal`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 1(2) the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought before the appointment` interp appointment MEANS
    CONSIDER appointment's `the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST sought THEN `Sch 1 and 2: the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought before an appointment` interp sought (appointment's `the day of the appointment`)

-- src:818 | (3) The Minister must, at least 2 weeks before appointing a person as a tribunal member, present to the States a notice of his or her intention to make the appointment.
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 1(3) (src:818)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 2 para 1(3) the notice of intention must be presented at least this many weeks before appointing` MEANS 2

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 1(3) (src:818)
@export The Minister's duty to present to the States a notice of intention at least 2 weeks before appointing a tribunal member
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      `the day of the appointment` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the appointment (or re-appointment) is made
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 2`
`Sch 2 para 1(3) at least 2 weeks before appointing a person as a tribunal member the Minister must present to the States a notice of intention` interp `the day of the appointment` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MUST `Sch 2: the Minister presents a notice of intention to the States to appoint a member`
    BEFORE (`Sch 1 and 2: the latest day for a notice of intention before an appointment` interp `the day of the appointment` `Sch 2 para 1(3) the notice of intention must be presented at least this many weeks before appointing`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not present to the States a notice of intention at least 2 weeks before appointing a person as a tribunal member"

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 1(3) (src:818)
@export Whether the notice of intention to appoint or re-appoint a member of the tribunal was presented to the States in time, that is at least 2 weeks before the appointment, counted as the chosen reading says
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      appointment IS AN `Appointment of a member of the tribunal` @desc The appointment or re-appointment and the dates of its steps
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 1(3) the notice of intention was presented to the States in time` interp appointment MEANS
    CONSIDER appointment's `a notice of intention was presented to the States on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST presented
        THEN `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of intention was presented in time before an appointment` interp presented (appointment's `the day of the appointment`) `Sch 2 para 1(3) the notice of intention must be presented at least this many weeks before appointing`

-- 1(4) is inert: it says the person holds and vacates the position in accordance with the terms of the appointment, subject to the Law. The terms of the appointment are not in the Law;
-- what the Law says about vacating the position is in paragraph 2, and the period is fixed by 1(5), so 1(4) adds no rule of its own.
-- src:819 | (4) A person appointed as a tribunal member holds and vacates that position in accordance with the terms of his or her appointment, subject to this Law.
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 1(4) (src:819)
`Sch 2 para 1(4) the terms of the appointment (inert)` MEANS
    "(4) A person appointed as a tribunal member holds and vacates that position in accordance with the terms of his or her appointment, subject to this Law."

-- src:820 | (5) When appointing a person as a tribunal member the Minister must determine the period of the appointment, being not more than 6 years.
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 1(5) (src:820)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 2 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is not more than this many years` MEANS 6

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 1(5) (src:820)
@export Whether the period the Minister determined for an appointment or re-appointment of a member of the tribunal is within the limit of not more than 6 years, counted as the chosen reading says
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      appointment IS AN `Appointment of a member of the tribunal` @desc The appointment or re-appointment, with its first day and the end date of its period
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` interp appointment MEANS
    `Sch 1 and 2: a term of an appointment is not more than that many years` interp (appointment's `the first day of the term`) (appointment's `the day the term expires`) `Sch 2 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is not more than this many years`

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 1(5) (src:820)
@export The Minister's duty, when appointing a tribunal member, to determine a period of the appointment of not more than 6 years
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      appointment IS AN `Appointment of a member of the tribunal` @desc The appointment or re-appointment, with the dates of its steps and the facts that bear on its expiry
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 2`
`Sch 2 para 1(5) when appointing a person as a tribunal member the Minister must determine the period of the appointment, being not more than 6 years` interp appointment MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MUST `Sch 2: the Minister determines the period of the appointment of a member`
    PROVIDED `Sch 2 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` interp appointment
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not determine a period of the appointment of a tribunal member of not more than 6 years"

-- src:821 | (6) The Minister may re-appoint a person serving as a tribunal member (and references in this paragraph to appointment include re-appointment).
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 1(6) (src:821)
@export The Minister's power to re-appoint a person serving as a tribunal member
GIVEN `the person is serving as a member of the tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the person to be re-appointed is serving as a member of the tribunal when the Minister re-appoints
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 2`
`Sch 2 para 1(6) the Minister may re-appoint a person serving as a tribunal member` `the person is serving as a member of the tribunal` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY `Sch 2: the Minister re-appoints a member serving`
    PROVIDED `the person is serving as a member of the tribunal`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

-- 1(6) also says that references in paragraph 1 to appointment include re-appointment, so the rules of 1(2), 1(3) and 1(5) above are asked of a re-appointment as of an appointment.

-- 1(7): among the members the Minister designates one as the chair and another as the vice-chair. The persons are named by STRINGs; the chair and the vice-chair must each be one of the members and must be different persons.
-- src:822 | (7) The Minister must, among the members of the tribunal, designate one as the chair and another as the vice-chair.
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 1(7) (src:822)
@export Whether one member of the tribunal is designated as the chair and another as the vice-chair, among the members
GIVEN members IS A LIST OF STRING @desc The names of the persons who are members of the tribunal on the day in question
      chair IS A MAYBE STRING @desc The name of the member designated as the chair, if any
      `vice-chair` IS A MAYBE STRING @desc The name of the member designated as the vice-chair, if any
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 1(7) one member is designated as the chair and another as the vice-chair` members chair `vice-chair` MEANS
    CONSIDER chair
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST first
        THEN CONSIDER `vice-chair`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST second
                 THEN     elem first members
                      AND elem second members
                      AND NOT (first EQUALS second)

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 1(7) (src:822)
@export The Minister's duty to designate one member of the tribunal as the chair and another as the vice-chair
GIVEN members IS A LIST OF STRING @desc The names of the persons who are members of the tribunal on the day in question
      chair IS A MAYBE STRING @desc The name of the member designated as the chair, if any
      `vice-chair` IS A MAYBE STRING @desc The name of the member designated as the vice-chair, if any
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 2`
`Sch 2 para 1(7) the Minister must designate one member as the chair and another as the vice-chair` members chair `vice-chair` MEANS
    IF `Sch 2 para 1(7) one member is designated as the chair and another as the vice-chair` members chair `vice-chair`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the Minister`
         MUST `Sch 2: the Minister designates the chair and the vice-chair`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not designate one member of the tribunal as the chair and another as the vice-chair"

-- 1(8): service is honorary unless the Minister determines that the chair is, or all the members are, to be remunerated by the States. The amount ("as Minister sees fit") is the Minister's: an input, not modelled.
-- src:823 | (8) Service as a tribunal member is honorary, unless the Minister determines that the chair is, or all the members are, to be remunerated by the States as Minister sees fit.
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 1(8) (src:823)
@export The Minister's power to determine that the chair, or all the members, of the tribunal are to be remunerated by the States
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 2`
`Sch 2 para 1(8) the Minister may determine that the chair is, or all the members are, to be remunerated by the States` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY `Sch 2: the Minister determines that the chair or all the members are to be remunerated`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

DECLARE `Determination of the Minister about remuneration of the tribunal` IS ONE OF
    `the Minister has determined nothing about remuneration`
    `the Minister has determined that the chair is to be remunerated by the States`
    `the Minister has determined that all the members are to be remunerated by the States`

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 1(8) (src:823)
@export Whether service as a tribunal member is honorary: it is, unless the Minister has determined that the chair is, or all the members are, to be remunerated by the States, and then it is not for the persons the determination covers
GIVEN determination IS A `Determination of the Minister about remuneration of the tribunal` @desc What the Minister has determined, if anything, about remuneration
      `the member is the chair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the member whose service is in question is the chair
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 1(8) service as a tribunal member is honorary` determination `the member is the chair` MEANS
    CONSIDER determination
    WHEN `the Minister has determined nothing about remuneration` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Minister has determined that the chair is to be remunerated by the States` THEN NOT `the member is the chair`
    WHEN `the Minister has determined that all the members are to be remunerated by the States` THEN FALSE

§§ `2 Termination of appointment`

-- A notice of resignation under 2(1)(a). `the day the resignation takes effect` is the first day on which the person is no longer a member, as the notice names it.
DECLARE `Notice of resignation of a member of the tribunal` HAS
    `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the member gave the notice
    `the notice is in writing and given to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the notice was in writing and given to the Minister
    `the day the resignation takes effect` IS A DATE @desc The first day on which the person is no longer a member, as the notice names it

-- The grounds of 2(2). The Minister's satisfaction on each ground is an input; the days of an absence are facts from which the Law's number (longer than 8 consecutive weeks) is computed.
-- F9.19 as in Schedule 1 paragraph 3(2).
DECLARE `Grounds for terminating the appointment of a member of the tribunal` HAS
    `the first day of absence from duties` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The first day of the absence of the person from his or her duties, if any
    `the last day of absence from duties` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The last day of that absence, if any
    `the Minister is satisfied that the person has been absent for a period longer than 8 consecutive weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Minister's satisfaction on ground (a): an input
    `the Minister is satisfied that the person has become bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Minister's satisfaction on ground (b): an input
    `the Minister is satisfied that the person is incapacitated by illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Minister's satisfaction on ground (c): an input
    `the Minister is satisfied that the person is otherwise unable or unfit to discharge the functions of a member of the tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Minister's satisfaction on ground (d): an input

-- A termination under 2(2).
DECLARE `Termination of the appointment of a member of the tribunal` HAS
    `the day the termination takes effect` IS A DATE @desc The first day on which the person is no longer a member because the Minister terminated the appointment
    grounds IS A `Grounds for terminating the appointment of a member of the tribunal` @desc The grounds on which the Minister terminated

-- What may have ended the position of a member (2(1)(a) and (b)); expiry (2(1)(c)) is computed from the appointment.
DECLARE `Events that may end the position of a member of the tribunal` HAS
    resignation IS A MAYBE `Notice of resignation of a member of the tribunal` @desc The notice of resignation, if the person gave one
    termination IS A MAYBE `Termination of the appointment of a member of the tribunal` @desc The termination by the Minister, if there was one

-- 2(1) is the chapeau of the three cases below, which are combined in the rule `Sch 2 para 2(1) the person has ceased to be a member of the tribunal by the day` at the end of this paragraph.
-- src:825 | (1) A person ceases to be a member of the tribunal if –
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 2(1) (src:825)
`Sch 2 para 2(1) a person ceases to be a member of the tribunal in these three cases (chapeau, inert)` MEANS
    "(1) A person ceases to be a member of the tribunal if –"

-- src:826 | (a) he or she resigns from office by giving not less than one month’s notice in writing to the Minister;
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 2(1)(a) (src:826)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 2 para 2(1)(a) the notice of resignation must be for not less than this many months` MEANS 1

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 2(1)(a) (src:826)
@export The first day on which a person is no longer a member of the tribunal because he or she resigned by giving not less than one month's notice in writing to the Minister, or NOTHING if the notice is not such a resignation
