-- 2(1)(b): the Minister terminates under 2(2), so the termination ends the position only if the Minister could terminate on the grounds (the gate is defined below, at 2(2)).
-- 2(1)(c): the appointment expires under 2(4) (defined below). Both are combined in the rule at the end of this paragraph.

-- 2(2) is a power of the Minister (encoded below as a MAY rule) whose chapeau is carried here and whose four grounds are encoded one by one.
-- src:829 | (2) The Minister may terminate the appointment of a person as a member of the tribunal, after satisfying himself or herself that the person –
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 2(2) (src:829)
`Sch 2 para 2(2) the Minister may terminate the appointment after satisfying himself or herself on one of four grounds (chapeau, inert)` MEANS
    "(2) The Minister may terminate the appointment of a person as a member of the tribunal, after satisfying himself or herself that the person –"

-- src:830 | (a) has been absent from his or her duties for a period longer than 8 consecutive weeks;
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 2(2)(a) (src:830)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 2 para 2(2)(a) the absence must be for a period longer than this many consecutive weeks` MEANS 8

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 2(2)(a) (src:830)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
      grounds IS A `Grounds for terminating the appointment of a member of the tribunal`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 2(2)(a) the person has been absent from duties for a period longer than 8 consecutive weeks` interp grounds MEANS
    CONSIDER grounds's `the first day of absence from duties`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST first
        THEN CONSIDER grounds's `the last day of absence from duties`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST last
                 THEN `Sch 1 and 2: an absence from duties was for a period longer than that many consecutive weeks` interp first last `Sch 2 para 2(2)(a) the absence must be for a period longer than this many consecutive weeks`

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 2(2)(a) (src:830)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
      grounds IS A `Grounds for terminating the appointment of a member of the tribunal`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 2(2)(a) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself that the person has been absent for a period longer than 8 consecutive weeks` interp grounds MEANS
    `Sch 1 and 2: the ground of absence for terminating an appointment is made out` interp (grounds's `the Minister is satisfied that the person has been absent for a period longer than 8 consecutive weeks`) (`Sch 2 para 2(2)(a) the person has been absent from duties for a period longer than 8 consecutive weeks` interp grounds)

-- src:831 | (b) has become bankrupt;
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 2(2)(b) (src:831)
