GIVEN grounds IS A `Grounds for terminating the appointment of a member of the tribunal`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 2(2)(d) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself that the person is otherwise unable or unfit to discharge the functions of a member of the tribunal` grounds MEANS
    grounds's `the Minister is satisfied that the person is otherwise unable or unfit to discharge the functions of a member of the tribunal`

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 2(2) (src:829-833)
@export Whether the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on at least one of the four grounds on which he or she may terminate the appointment of a member of the tribunal
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      grounds IS A `Grounds for terminating the appointment of a member of the tribunal` @desc The days of any absence and the Minister's satisfaction on each of the four grounds
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 2(2) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on a ground for terminating` interp grounds MEANS
        "(a)" ... `Sch 2 para 2(2)(a) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself that the person has been absent for a period longer than 8 consecutive weeks` interp grounds
    OR  "(b)" ... `Sch 2 para 2(2)(b) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself that the person has become bankrupt` grounds
    OR  "(c)" ... `Sch 2 para 2(2)(c) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself that the person is incapacitated by illness` grounds
    OR  "(d)" ... `Sch 2 para 2(2)(d) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself that the person is otherwise unable or unfit to discharge the functions of a member of the tribunal` grounds

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 2(2) (src:829-833)
@export The Minister's power to terminate the appointment of a tribunal member after satisfying himself or herself on one of four grounds
