@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 2(4) (src:835)
`Sch 2 para 2(4) a person's appointment as a member of the tribunal expires in these three cases (chapeau, inert)` MEANS
    "(4) A person’s appointment as a member of the tribunal expires if –"

-- 2(4)(a): the period expires without re-appointment. If the term is followed by a re-appointment its end is not an expiry (the person goes on under the next appointment).
-- src:836 | (a) the period for which the person was appointed expires without re-appointment;
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 2(4)(a) (src:836)
GIVEN appointment IS AN `Appointment of a member of the tribunal`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Sch 2 para 2(4)(a) the day the period of the appointment expires without re-appointment` appointment MEANS
    IF appointment's `the term is followed by a re-appointment`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (appointment's `the day the term expires`)

-- 2(4)(b): the person becomes a member of the States. F9.17 as in Schedule 1 paragraph 3(4)(b).
-- src:837 | (b) the person becomes a member of the States; or
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 2(4)(b) (src:837)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
      appointment IS AN `Appointment of a member of the tribunal`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Sch 2 para 2(4)(b) the day the person becomes a member of the States` interp appointment MEANS
    `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which membership of the States ends the appointment` interp (appointment's `the day on which the person became a member of the States`) (appointment's `the first day of the term`)

