    `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which twelve years of service are completed` interp (appointment's `the service before this appointment`) (appointment's `the first day of the term`)

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 2(4) (src:835-838)
@export The first day on which the appointment of a member of the tribunal has expired under paragraph 2(4): when the period of the appointment runs out without re-appointment, when the person becomes a member of the States, or when the person completes 12 years of service as a member, whichever is first
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      appointment IS AN `Appointment of a member of the tribunal` @desc The appointment, the periods of service before it and any membership of the States
GIVETH A DATE
`Sch 2 para 2(4) the day on which the appointment expires` interp appointment MEANS
    CONSIDER `Sch 1 and 2: the earlier of two optional days` (`Sch 2 para 2(4)(a) the day the period of the appointment expires without re-appointment` appointment) (`Sch 2 para 2(4)(b) the day the person becomes a member of the States` interp appointment)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `Sch 2 para 2(4)(c) the day the person completes 12 years of service as a member of the tribunal` interp appointment
    WHEN JUST earlier THEN `Sch 1 and 2: the earlier of two days` earlier (`Sch 2 para 2(4)(c) the day the person completes 12 years of service as a member of the tribunal` interp appointment)

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 2(4) (src:835-838)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
      appointment IS AN `Appointment of a member of the tribunal`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 2(4) the appointment has expired by the day` interp appointment `the day` MEANS
    `the day` AT LEAST `Sch 2 para 2(4) the day on which the appointment expires` interp appointment

-- src:827 | (b) the Minister terminates his or her appointment under sub-paragraph (2); or
-- src:828 | (c) his or her appointment expires under sub-paragraph (4).
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 2(1)(b) and (c) (src:827-828)
@export Whether a person has ceased to be a member of the tribunal by the day in question: by resigning on not less than one month's notice in writing, by the Minister's termination under paragraph 2(2), or by expiry under paragraph 2(4)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      appointment IS AN `Appointment of a member of the tribunal` @desc The appointment in force and the facts that bear on its expiry
      events IS AN `Events that may end the position of a member of the tribunal` @desc Any notice of resignation and any termination by the Minister
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is asked
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 2(1) the person has ceased to be a member of the tribunal by the day` interp appointment events `the day` MEANS
        "(a)" ... `Sch 2 para 2(1)(a) the person has resigned by the day` interp events `the day`
    OR  "(b)" ... `Sch 2 para 2(1)(b) the Minister has terminated the appointment by the day` interp events `the day`
    OR  "(c)" ... `Sch 2 para 2(4) the appointment has expired by the day` interp appointment `the day`

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 2(1)(a) (src:826)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
      events IS AN `Events that may end the position of a member of the tribunal`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 2(1)(a) the person has resigned by the day` interp events `the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER events's resignation
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST notice
        THEN CONSIDER `Sch 2 para 2(1)(a) the day the position ends by resignation` interp notice
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST ends THEN `the day` AT LEAST ends

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 2(1)(b) (src:827)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
      events IS AN `Events that may end the position of a member of the tribunal`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 2(1)(b) the Minister has terminated the appointment by the day` interp events `the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER events's termination
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST termination
        THEN     `Sch 2 para 2(2) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on a ground for terminating` interp (termination's grounds)
             AND `the day` AT LEAST termination's `the day the termination takes effect`

§§ `3 Staff, resources and reporting`

-- What the Minister has made available to the tribunal (3(1)). The number and descriptions of staff and the resources the Minister considers are required are the Minister's consideration: an input.
DECLARE `Staff and resources made available to the tribunal` HAS
    `the number of staff the Minister considers are required` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of staff the Minister considers are required for the proper and effective discharge of the tribunal's functions: an input
    `the number of staff made available` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of staff the Minister has made available to the tribunal
    `the descriptions of staff made available are those the Minister considers are required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the descriptions of staff made available match those the Minister considers are required: an input
    `the resources made available are those the Minister considers are required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the resources made available are those the Minister considers are required: an input

-- src:840 | (1) The Minister must make available to the tribunal such number and descriptions of staff and resources as the Minister considers are required for the proper and effective discharge of the tribunal’s functions.
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 3(1) (src:840)
GIVEN provision IS A `Staff and resources made available to the tribunal`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 3(1) the Minister has made available the number and descriptions of staff and the resources that the Minister considers are required` provision MEANS
        provision's `the number of staff made available` AT LEAST provision's `the number of staff the Minister considers are required`
    AND provision's `the descriptions of staff made available are those the Minister considers are required`
    AND provision's `the resources made available are those the Minister considers are required`

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 3(1) (src:840)
@export The Minister's duty to make available to the tribunal the staff and resources that the Minister considers are required
GIVEN provision IS A `Staff and resources made available to the tribunal` @desc What the Minister has made available: the number considered required, the number made available, whether the descriptions match, and whether the resources match
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 2`
`Sch 2 para 3(1) the Minister must make available to the tribunal such number and descriptions of staff and resources as the Minister considers are required` provision MEANS
    IF `Sch 2 para 3(1) the Minister has made available the number and descriptions of staff and the resources that the Minister considers are required` provision
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the Minister`
         MUST `Sch 2: the Minister makes staff and resources available to the tribunal`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not make available to the tribunal the number and descriptions of staff and the resources that the Minister considers are required for the proper and effective discharge of the tribunal's functions"

-- 3(2): at least one member of staff is available to serve as the responsible officer, charged with assisting with the administration of the tribunal but not with determinations by it.
DECLARE `Matter of the tribunal` IS ONE OF
    `the administration of the tribunal`
    `a determination by the tribunal`

-- src:841 | (2) The Minister must secure that there is available to the tribunal at least one member of staff to serve as the responsible officer, charged with assisting with the administration of (but not determinations by) the tribunal.
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 3(2) (src:841)
@export Whether the Minister has secured that at least one member of staff is available to the tribunal as the responsible officer, charged with assisting with the administration of (but not determinations by) the tribunal
GIVEN `the number of members of staff available to the tribunal to serve as the responsible officer` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of members of staff available to the tribunal to serve as the responsible officer
      `the responsible officer is charged with assisting with the administration of the tribunal and not with determinations by it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the responsible officer is charged with assisting with the administration of the tribunal and not with determinations by it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 3(2) at least one member of staff is available to the tribunal as the responsible officer` `the number of members of staff available to the tribunal to serve as the responsible officer` `the responsible officer is charged with assisting with the administration of the tribunal and not with determinations by it` MEANS
        `the number of members of staff available to the tribunal to serve as the responsible officer` AT LEAST 1
    AND `the responsible officer is charged with assisting with the administration of the tribunal and not with determinations by it`

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 3(2) (src:841)
GIVEN matter IS A `Matter of the tribunal`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 3(2) the responsible officer is charged with assisting with the matter` matter MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `the administration of the tribunal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a determination by the tribunal` THEN FALSE

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 3(2) (src:841)
@export The Minister's duty to secure that at least one member of staff is available to the tribunal as the responsible officer
GIVEN `the number of members of staff available to the tribunal to serve as the responsible officer` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of members of staff available to the tribunal to serve as the responsible officer
      `the responsible officer is charged with assisting with the administration of the tribunal and not with determinations by it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the responsible officer is charged with assisting with the administration of the tribunal and not with determinations by it
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 2`
`Sch 2 para 3(2) the Minister must secure that at least one member of staff is available to the tribunal as the responsible officer` `the number of members of staff available to the tribunal to serve as the responsible officer` `the responsible officer is charged with assisting with the administration of the tribunal and not with determinations by it` MEANS
    IF `Sch 2 para 3(2) at least one member of staff is available to the tribunal as the responsible officer` `the number of members of staff available to the tribunal to serve as the responsible officer` `the responsible officer is charged with assisting with the administration of the tribunal and not with determinations by it`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the Minister`
         MUST `Sch 2: the Minister secures a responsible officer for the tribunal`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not secure that at least one member of staff is available to the tribunal to serve as the responsible officer"

-- 3(2) says "at least one member of staff to serve as the responsible officer", and 3(3) to (5) then speak of "the responsible officer" in the singular: with several members of staff available the Law does not say who
-- the responsible officer is. F9.18, reading A (taken): the responsible officer is the one member of staff the Minister has named (an input); with one member of staff available that member is the responsible officer;
-- with several available and none named the Law does not answer. Reading B: every member of staff available is the responsible officer.
-- src:841 | (2) The Minister must secure that there is available to the tribunal at least one member of staff to serve as the responsible officer, charged with assisting with the administration of (but not determinations by) the tribunal.
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 3(2) (src:841)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
      staff IS A LIST OF STRING @desc The names of the members of staff available to the tribunal to serve as the responsible officer
      named IS A MAYBE STRING @desc The name of the member of staff the Minister has named as the responsible officer, if any (an input: the Law does not say how the responsible officer is named)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Sch 2 para 3(2) the members of staff who are the responsible officer` interp staff named MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `the responsible officer where several members of staff are available`
    WHEN `the one member of staff the Minister has named is the responsible officer`
        THEN `F9.18 reading A: the one member of staff the Minister has named is the responsible officer` staff named
    WHEN `every member of staff available is the responsible officer`
        THEN `F9.18 reading B: every member of staff available is the responsible officer` staff named

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 3(2) (src:841)
GIVEN staff IS A LIST OF STRING
      named IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`F9.18 reading A: the one member of staff the Minister has named is the responsible officer` staff named MEANS
    CONSIDER staff
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN only FOLLOWED BY EMPTY THEN LIST only
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest
        THEN CONSIDER named
             WHEN NOTHING
                 THEN REFUSE "paragraph 3(2) provides for at least one member of staff to serve as the responsible officer and does not say who the responsible officer is where several are available and none is named"
             WHEN JUST chosen
                 THEN IF elem chosen staff
                      THEN LIST chosen
                      ELSE REFUSE "the member of staff named as the responsible officer is not one of the members of staff available to the tribunal"

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 3(2) (src:841)
GIVEN staff IS A LIST OF STRING
      named IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`F9.18 reading B: every member of staff available is the responsible officer` staff named MEANS
    staff

-- The report (3(3) to (5)): the responsible officer prepares it and provides it to the Minister; the Minister lays a copy before the States. "As soon as practicable" is fork F9.10.
DECLARE `Report on the tribunal for a calendar year` HAS
    `the calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year the report relates to
    `the responsible officer has prepared the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the responsible officer has prepared the report on the activities of the tribunal in the year
    `the day on which the report was provided to the Minister` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc NOTHING if the responsible officer has not provided the report to the Minister
    `the report was provided as soon as practicable after the end of the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The determination that the responsible officer provided the report as soon as practicable (an input, used by the reading of F9.10 that takes it as a judgement)
    `the day on which the Minister laid a copy before the States` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc NOTHING if the Minister has not laid a copy before the States
    `the copy was laid as soon as practicable after the Minister received the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The determination that the Minister laid the copy as soon as practicable (an input, used by the reading of F9.10 that takes it as a judgement)

-- src:842 | (3) The responsible officer must prepare a report on the activities of the tribunal in each calendar year.
@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 3(3) (src:842)
@export The responsible officer's duty to prepare a report on the activities of the tribunal in a calendar year in which he or she held the post
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      `the first day on which the post was held` IS A DATE @desc The first day on which the person held the post of responsible officer
      `the last day on which the post was held` IS A DATE @desc The last day on which the person held the post of responsible officer
      `the calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year the report relates to
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role under Schedule 2` `Act of a member or the responsible officer under Schedule 2`
`Sch 2 para 3(3) the responsible officer must prepare a report on the activities of the tribunal in each calendar year` interp `the first day on which the post was held` `the last day on which the post was held` `the calendar year` MEANS
    IF `Sch 1 and 2: a report is required of the holder for a calendar year` interp `the first day on which the post was held` `the last day on which the post was held` `the calendar year`
    THEN PARTY `the responsible officer of the tribunal under Schedule 2`
         MUST `Sch 2: the responsible officer prepares the report`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the responsible officer of the tribunal under Schedule 2` BECAUSE "the responsible officer did not prepare a report on the activities of the tribunal in the calendar year"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:843 | (4) The responsible officer must provide the Minister with the report as soon as practicable after the end of the year to which the report relates, but in no case later than 4 months after the end of that year.
