    `Sch 1 and 2: the last day for a step that is to be taken as soon as practicable and in no case after a day` interp (YMD `the calendar year` 12 31) (`Sch 1 and 2: the latest day for a report on a calendar year` interp `the calendar year` `Sch 2 para 3(4) the report must be provided in no case later than this many months after the end of the year`)

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 3(4) (src:843)
@export The responsible officer's duty to provide the Minister with the report on a calendar year as soon as practicable after the year ends and in no case later than 4 months after it
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      `the calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year the report relates to
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role under Schedule 2` `Act of a member or the responsible officer under Schedule 2`
`Sch 2 para 3(4) the responsible officer must provide the Minister with the report as soon as practicable after the end of the year, and in no case later than 4 months after it` interp `the calendar year` MEANS
    PARTY `the responsible officer of the tribunal under Schedule 2`
    MUST `Sch 2: the responsible officer provides the Minister with the report`
    BEFORE (`Sch 2 para 3(4) the last day for providing the Minister with the report` interp `the calendar year`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the responsible officer of the tribunal under Schedule 2` BECAUSE "the responsible officer did not provide the Minister with the report as soon as practicable after the end of the year, and in no case later than 4 months after it"

@ref Schedule 2 paragraph 3(4) (src:843)
@export Whether the responsible officer provided the Minister with the report on the tribunal for a calendar year in time: as soon as practicable after the end of the year, and in no case later than 4 months after it (30 April on the favoured reading)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      report IS A `Report on the tribunal for a calendar year` @desc The report, the year it relates to and the day it was provided to the Minister
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 3(4) the responsible officer provided the Minister with the report in time` interp report MEANS
    CONSIDER report's `the day on which the report was provided to the Minister`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST provided
        THEN     `Sch 1 and 2: a report was provided within that many months after the end of the year` interp (report's `the calendar year`) provided `Sch 2 para 3(4) the report must be provided in no case later than this many months after the end of the year`
             AND `Sch 1 and 2: a step was taken as soon as practicable` interp (report's `the report was provided as soon as practicable after the end of the year`) (YMD (report's `the calendar year`) 12 31) provided

-- src:844 | (5) The Minister must lay a copy of the report so provided before the States as soon as practicable after the Minister receives the report.
